<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Tangent Plane and Normal Line Calculation for a Given Equation</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the following equation, we need to find the tangent plane and the normal line.</p>
<p>\({@question_expr@}\) at \(({@point_x@},{@point_y@},{@point_z@})\)</p>
<p><b>Step </b>\(1\): Let us rewrite the equation as follows,</p>
<p>\({@function@}\) </p>
<p>From here we need to differentiate the equation implicitly to find the gradient function.</p>
<p>(Hint: Find the derivative with respect to \(x, y\) and \(z\) respectively for the inputs below) </p>
<br>
<p>\(\triangledown f_x=\)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>\(\triangledown f_y=\)[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>\(\triangledown f_z=\)[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]][[feedback:prt3]]</p>

<p><b>Step </b>\(2:\)  Now, find the gradient  at the points \(({@point_x@},{@point_y@},{@point_z@})\) using the gradient functions you have found in Step 1 above</p>
<p> (Hint: Substitute for \(x,y\) \(z\) in the gradient functions above)</p>
<p>\(\triangledown f_x=\)[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]][[feedback:prt4]]</p>
<p>\(\triangledown f_y=\)[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]][[feedback:prt5]]</p>
<p>\(\triangledown f_z=\)[[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans6]][[feedback:prt6]]</p>

<p><b>Step </b>\(3:\)Now find the equation of the tangent plane.</p>
<p>\(\triangledown f_x(x-x_1)+\triangledown f_y(y-y_1)+\triangledown f_z(z-z_1)\)</p>
<p>\(=\) [[input:ans7]] [[validation:ans7]][[feedback:prt7]]</p>

<p><b>Step </b>\(4:\) We can find the normal line given</p>
<p>\(\vec{r}(t)=( x_1,x_2,x_3) +t(\triangledown f_x, \triangledown f_y,\triangledown f_z)\)</p>
<p>\(\vec{r}(t)=\) [[input:ans8]][[validation:ans8]][[feedback:prt8]]</p>
<p></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked solution</b></p>
<p>Given \(\displaystyle{@question_expr@} \), we need to solve the problem as follows,</p>
<p><b>Step </b>\(1\): The first thing will be to rewrite the equation as shown,</p>
<p>{@function@}</p>
<p>We need to compute \(\displaystyle\frac{d f(x,y,z)}{dx})=\triangledown f_x, \frac{d f(x,y,z)}{dy})=\triangledown f_y, \frac{d f(x,y,z)}{dz})=\triangledown f_z\). </p>
<br>
<p>\(\displaystyle \triangledown f_x={@ta_1@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \triangledown f_y= {@ta_2@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle  \triangledown f_z= {@ta_3@}\)</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Step </b>\(2:\)  Now, we can find the gradient  at the points \(({@point_x@},{@point_y@},{@point_z@})\) by substituting for the values of \(x,y,z\) respectively to the  above equation \(\displaystyle \triangledown f_x,\triangledown f_y,\triangledown f_z\)   
<p>\(\displaystyle \triangledown f_x={@ta_4@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \triangledown f_y={@ta_5@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \triangledown f_z={@ta_6@}\)</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Step </b>\(3:\)Now to  find the equation of the tangent plane,we need to do as follows,</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle  \triangledown f_x(x-x_1)+\triangledown f_y(y-y_1)+\triangledown f_z(z-z_1)={@tangent@}\)</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Step </b>\(4:\) We now find the normal line given the guide equation below,</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle  r^\rightarrow (t)=( x_1,x_2,x_3)+t(\triangledown f_x, \triangledown f_y,\triangledown f_z)= ({@point_x@},{@point_y@},{@point_z@})+ t({@ta_4@},{@ta_5@},{@ta_6@} )\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle  r^\rightarrow (t)= ( {@ta_8@} ) \) </p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
